  "body": "I'm nearly done switching Bikeshed over to using [WebRef](https://github.com/w3c/webref) as its definition source, and just checking over the results before I throw the switch.\r\n\r\nOne particular issue I've noticed is that Shepherd, when it found a single `dfn` without an ID in a heading element, would report the heading's ID for the `dfn`. This gave good results for HTML, which has several of these, such as <https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/structured-data.html#serializable-objects>. \r\n\r\nWebRef doesn't do this, and so these terms no longer show up in the database. Either these `dfn`s need to gain IDs, or we need to carry over this HTML special case to WebRef.\r\n\r\n(No Bikeshed or ReSpec spec needs it, since both tools ensure that every dfn has an ID.)",
